**Place:** Kyiv, Ukraine
**Starting date:** 01/12/2026
**Duration of contract:** 6 months
**Closing date for applications:** November 15th, 2026

Humanity & Inclusion is an independent and impartial aid organisation working in situations of poverty and exclusion, conflict and disaster. The organisation works alongside people with disabilities and vulnerable populations, taking action and bearing witness in order to respond to their essential needs, improve their living conditions and promote respect for their dignity and fundamental rights.

Since its creation in 1982, HI has run development & humanitarian projects in more than 55 countries and responded to numerous emergencies. Today, we have a budget of approximately 200 million euros, with 4,000 employees worldwide

At Handicap International-Humanity & Inclusion, we truly believe in the importance of inclusion and diversity within our organisation. This is why we are engaged to a disability policy to encourage the inclusion and integration of people with disabilities.

Please indicate if you require any special accommodation, even at the first interview. [For more information about the organisation.](https://www.hi.org/en/index)

**JOB CONTEXT:**
From February 2022, HI has re-opened a Country Programme in Ukraine to respond to the humanitarian needs triggered by the full-scale invasion of Ukraine by the Russian Federation.

In 2024, HI pillars of interventions are:

- Health: HI aims to improve access to quality physical rehabilitation and mental health and psychosocial support services (MHPSS) for conflict-affected vulnerable population;
- Protection: Given the scale of humanitarian and protection needs, HI intervenes at various levels to ensure that vulnerable conflict-affected populations have access to multi-sectoral services tailored to their needs. In addition, HI aims to foster a disability-inclusive humanitarian response;
- Humanitarian Mine Action: Ongoing attacks dangerously exacerbated Explosive Ordnance (EO) contamination in Ukraine:
- EORE/CPP: HI is conducting a multi-pronged approach to EO Risk Education (RE) and Conflict Preparedness and Protection (CPP);
- Advocacy;
- NTS: HI is implementing Non-Technical Survey activities in Kharkivska Oblast since 2025;
- VA (Victim Assistance).

HI has 2 hubs, one in the East (based in Dnipro), one in the North East (based in Kharkiv), and the coordination office is in Kyiv.

**YOUR MISSION:**

Under the responsibility of the Technical Unit Regional Manager, the Field Technical Specialist contributes within the country where he/she is based to the implementation of the mandate and the 10-year strategy of Humanity & Inclusion. He/she ensures optimal quality and impact of the projects implemented in the country, through a delegation system with appropriate control mechanisms. He/she contributes to the sound management and successful functionning of the overall organisation through paradigm shifts.

**Responsibilities**

**Expertise**

- Contribute to the regional strategies in line with the global strategies;
- Ensure technical support to projects in line with the global technical frameworks and standards in his/her sectorial scope;
- Ensure technical learning from projects;
- Control & monitor the technical quality and the relevance of HI’s activities in the Programmes under his/her scope;
- Ensure compliance of the technical proposition with nexus stakes;
- Contribute to the development of research and innovation projects in the region when relevant, in his/her sectorial scope;
- Contribute to the Technical Divisions professional channel facilitation within the Program.

**Influence:** Contribute to the local external prestige and influence of HI’s expertise in his sectorial scope:

- Represent the technical expertise of HI throughout the local relevant networks (Sectorial Representation);
- Contribute to advocacy on specific themes in line with the global advocacy priorities;
- Contribute to communication messages locally in line with the global communication priorities.

**Business development:** Ensure the development of major opportunities or new projects in the region under his/her sectorial scope:

- Lead or contribute to the context analysis in his sectorial scope;
- Lead or contribute to the design and writing of new projects in the region and when asked in other countries within the Geographic Division;
- Identify & transform major opportunities in the region under his scope;
- Identify & develop local partnerships and/or consortium with NGOs, Institutions,
- Companies on technical priorities or important topics in the region under his sectorial scope;
- Contribute to the conception of major projects (multiple countries, one theme) or of new projects in the region.

**Emergency preparedness and response responsibilities**

- Contribute to the support or implementation of emergency preparedness actions of the programme(s) and, during an emergency, adapts his/her working modality to contribute to an effective HI humanitarian response.

**CHARACTERISTICS OF THE POSITION:**

The security situation in Ukraine remains relatively stable, although air alert is frequently active. However, markets, restaurants and cafes are open, and life continues as normal. There is a strict curfew, the hours depend on the region.

**YOUR PROFILE:**

- Degree in physical therapy and/or occupational therapy ;
- At least 5 years of overall professional experience with 3 years of experience in the rehab sector in conflict-affected countries ;
- Experience in developing and designing rehabilitation strategies/ policies/guidelines ;
- Strong interpersonal and intercultural skills.

**CONDITIONS:**
At HI, the conditions offered are up to your commitment and adapted to the context of your mission: [Join the team](https://hi.org/en/join-the-team)

- **6 months International contract** starting from December 1st, 2026;
- The international contract provides social cover adapted to your situation:
- Unemployment insurance benefits for EU nationals;
- Pension scheme;
- Medical coverage with 50% of employee contribution;
- Repatriation insurance paid by HI;
- Salary from 2757€ gross/month upon experience;
- Perdiem: 597€ net/month - paid in payroll;
- Hardship: 500 € net/month paid with your salary;
- Paid leaves: 25 days per year;
- R&R: 5 days every 8 weeks => + possible transport/package support;
- Position **Unaccompanied:**
- Housing: Collective taken in charge by HI;
- If you are resident in the country: local package.

**Job Title: People and Culture/HR Coordinator**

**Work Location: Syria, Damascus**

**Position Summary**

The People and Culture Coordinator is a key contributor to the P&C team ensuring effective and consistent delivery of P&C service. This role will work closely with Head of P&C in the implementation of CO P&C policies, procedures, approaches and practices in line with CARE People and Culture Strategy. The employee is required to collaborate with other P&C teams in implementing various people and culture operational functions across all offices in Syria which includes but not limited to recruitment and selection, compensation and benefits administration, performance management, safeguarding, learning and development, employee engagement and HR compliance.

The employee is also required to;

1\. Remain aware of and comply with safety and security regulations/procedures and bear responsibility for personal safety and security while under contract.

2\. Comply with CARE Policies which includes but not limited to Safeguarding Policy, Code of Conduct and other organizational and P&C policies.

3\. The organization has a zero-tolerance approach towards sexual harassment, exploitation and abuse, and child abuse towards any person including our staff, representatives, partners, programme participants and members of the community where we work. We expect all staff, partners and related personnel to share this commitment by understanding, abiding by and working within the organization International Safeguarding Policy and related framework at all times whilst representing the organization.

4\. Ensure that all direct team members are aware of their responsibilities with the CI Safeguarding Policy commitments, including signing of the Safeguarding Policy and Code of Conduct, and completing induction and refresher trainings;

5\. Depending on specific role and responsibilities, may be requested to comply with the terms of additional policies, guidelines and related regulations, as and when necessary.

**Key Responsibilities**

**Implement P&C recruitment strategies and policies**

- Managing the end-to-end process for various recruiting workflows (from requests, leading recruitment strategy meetings, job posting, longlisting, scheduling tests/interviews, reference checks and onboarding);
- Support the success of CARE recruitment strategy through contribution to strategic projects/initiatives
- Follow up with the recruitment request approval process ensuring it is in line with the recruitment plan;
- Collaborate with various departments and provide the P&C advice and support to ensure a seamless candidate experience;
- Ensure all recruitments have an updated job description that reflect the current needs as well as clear defined selection criteria to support the selection of the right talent to contribute to organizational goals and objectives;
- Ensure all candidates receive timely feedback after each recruitment stage ensuring effective communication for each step;
- Prepare the offer letters for new joiners and employees changing positions after a successful recruitment process and ensure approval by Head of P&C.
- Maintain an up-to-date industry knowledge on recruitment strategies and approaches;
- Work with hiring managers to ensure smooth and timely implementation of recruitment and selection processes are fair, fit and inclusive;
- Regular training of employees with line management responsibilities to ensure the consistency in recruitment practices and approach.

**Implement P&C strategies, policies and procedures including participation in P&C reports**

- In collaboration with Head of P&C, monitor the implementation and compliance of P&C policies, SoPs and procedures including monitoring all P&C related activities to ensure P&C team compliance;
- Facilitate and continuously improve employee engagement activities in collaboration with the Staff Committee;
- Act as a resource for employees and managers to resolve workplace issues in a fair and equitable manner, providing advise on conflict resolution, disciplinary actions, duty of care and organizational policies to ensure consistent application;
- Facilitate regular employee relations and ensure employees are aware of grievance procedure and appropriate actions are taken and documented;
- Liaise with other NGOs working in country to compare policies and establish best practices and also keep up to date on P&C trends;
- Support successful implementation of People and Culture strategy through contribution to strategic P&C projects/initiatives;
- In close collaboration with Head of P&C support the implementation and compliance of safeguarding policy.
- Promote to ensure safer P&C practices are consistently applied in all P&C cycle;
- Act as P&C focal point for P&C related Partners Management;
- Work closely with Procurement Team in P&C Service Provider Request, Assessment and Selection.

**Facilitate and Implement CARE learning and development strategies and programs**

- Implement CARE L&D strategy that aligns with the operational needs of the CO.
- Work closely with various departments across the organization and having a full understanding of their units and training requirements.
- Ensure baseline training documents and learning activities are produced, maintained and available for the concerned departments and effectively used.
- Follow up to ensure allocated budget are well utilized in collaboration with Finance.
- Conduct training needs assessment to identify gap and develop training plans.
- Follow up to ensure capacity strengthening of staff to deliver high quality programs in response to humanitarian needs.
- Promote a culture of continuous learning and development within CARE Syria.
- Partner with external training provider in collaboration with Procurement team to enhance staff skills and knowledge.
- Develop and implement and evaluation framework to measure effectiveness of training programs.
- Track and report on key metrics related to learning and development which includes but not limited to training evaluation, satisfaction and impact.
- Facilitate knowledge sharing across the organization to promote learning and innovation.

**Implement employee’s performance management to support learning and development**

- Facilitate the entire performance management cycle (from goal setting, midterm review and performance review) following CARE Global Performance Management Framework and Approaches;
- Using CARE global performance tools and resources, conduct periodic refreshers training for managers and other categories of employees when required;
- Collaborate with Head of P&C as well as line managers to ensure that the learning and development initiatives, needs and opportunities of employees are clearly identified, and possible options discussed and implemented;
- Facilitate annual refreshers training on P&C policies and practices including safeguarding related to P&C

**Required:**

- Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or a related field
- 5 years of experience as an HR/P&C Generalist or in a similar role;
- Excellent interpersonal, communication, and conflict-resolution skills;
- Ability to handle sensitive information with integrity and confidentiality.
- Capacity to demonstrate CARE Core competencies and values;
- Strong organizational and time-management skills;
- Emotional and culturally intelligent to collaborate and work in a diverse team;
- Analytical and problem solving skills.

**Safeguarding Commitments**

The organization has a zero-tolerance approach toward sexual harassment, exploitation and abuse, and child abuse. We will carefully examine allegations and investigate, and take appropriate disciplinary action where this is needed, taking into consideration the rights and interests of the survivor, consistent with the organization’s survivor-centred approach. We make very clear that sexual harassment, exploitation and abuse, and child abuse in any form, perpetrated by our staff, partners or other related personnel, towards anyone, will not be tolerated.

We provide equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, handicap, disability, or marital status.

## **Scope of Services**

**Nature of Services:** Independent Project Management Consultancy Services

**Place of Performance:** Such location as determined by the Consultant when performing the Services subject to any location-specific requirements expressly agreed in writing for a particular assignment.

**Level of Effort:** Assignment-based and strictly as mutually agreed in writing for specific tasks and deliverables. No minimum number of days/hours, fixed working hours, or continuing level of effort is guaranteed or required.

**Type of Contract:** Services will be provided on a day-rate basis against specific project assignments, deliverables, and estimated levels of effort agreed between COAR and the Consultant.

**Timeframe:** The anticipated term of this consultancy is from 01 December 2026 to 31 December 2027, subject to execution of the applicable agreement. The term establishes the period during which assignments may be agreed; it does not create an obligation to provide or accept assignments, guarantee a minimum workload, or require continuous availability. Any extension shall be subject to mutual written agreement.

**Primary Point of Contact:** COAR's designated Senior Programs Manager, acting as the contact for agreeing assignment requirements, coordinating necessary project inputs, clarifying deliverables, addressing technical queries and reviewing completed outputs against the agreed scope. This role is for assignment coordination and does not confer authority to direct the Consultant's day-to-day working methods or exercise line-management authority over the Consultant.

### Overview

This Scope of Services (SoS) outlines the Project Management Consultancy services with the Center for Operational Analysis and Research (COAR). The Consultant will provide independent professional services in relation to specifically commissioned project-management assignments. Depending on the scope of an accepted assignment, these services may include preparing project plans and coordination materials, analysing project budgets and resource requirements, identifying delivery risks and dependencies, documenting client feedback, and making recommendations concerning project implementation and delivery. The Consultant shall be responsible for the agreed consultancy outputs and coordination activities, but shall not assume general responsibility for managing COAR's personnel, organisational operations, or projects beyond the scope of an accepted assignment. The Consultant will liaise with technical, research, and support colleagues as reasonably necessary to perform the agreed Services. The Consultant may coordinate specified project inputs, communicate agreed project requirements and timelines, identify risks and constraints, and provide recommendations to COAR concerning actions that may support delivery of the relevant project scope. COAR and its personnel shall retain responsibility for organisational decisions, personnel management, and approvals falling outside the Consultant's expressly agreed authority.

### Nature of the consultancy

This is an independent, non-exclusive, project-based consultancy engagement and not a position of employment with COAR. Services will be commissioned through specific assignments agreed between COAR and the Consultant, setting out the relevant scope, deliverables, estimated level of effort, timeframe and applicable day rate.

COAR does not guarantee any minimum number of assignments or consultancy days, and the Consultant will remain free to accept or decline proposed assignments and to provide services to other clients, subject to confidentiality, conflicts of interest and the timely delivery of any assignment accepted.

The Consultant will determine independently the professional approach, methods, sequencing, working time and place of performance of the Services, subject to agreed deliverables, deadlines, applicable legal, contractual, client, security, safeguarding, confidentiality and other project-specific requirements and reasonable project coordination. The Consultant will ordinarily use their own equipment and working facilities and will be responsible for their own tax, social insurance and other statutory obligations arising from the consultancy. The consultancy does not carry employee benefits.

The Consultant will coordinate their own activities and agreed project inputs but will not occupy a position within COAR’s organisational structure, exercise employment or line-management authority over COAR personnel, or have authority to bind COAR, except where expressly authorised in writing for a defined project purpose.

Fees will be payable only for Services performed under an agreed assignment and against submission of appropriate invoices. No minimum volume of work or continuing retainer is guaranteed.

### About COAR

COAR is an independent social enterprise that directly supports practitioners, policymakers, and donors by facilitating humanitarian and development interventions in complex, fragile, and high-risk environments.

### Objectives

- To provide independent project management services in connection with the set-up, implementation, and close-out of specifically assigned projects;
- To support the timely delivery of assigned projects within agreed budgets and in accordance with applicable contractual requirements, client expectations, and those COAR policies and standards reasonably applicable to external consultants and relevant to the delivery of the Services ;
- To provide project-level coordination of agreed resources, risks, and operational requirements to support efficient and high-quality delivery;
- To facilitate, where relevant to an agreed assignment, communication between COAR and its clients, partners, and other relevant stakeholders; and
- Where separately agreed in writing, provide defined proposal-development or business-development consultancy outputs relating to the Consultant’s professional expertise

### Activities

#### **Project Management**

- Prepare and maintain project coordination materials identifying the agreed scope, deliverables, timelines, dependencies and allocation of project inputs;
- Develop and maintain project workplans and systems for assigned projects, providing relevant COAR personnel with visibility of priorities, progress, risks, and decisions and making recommendations regarding actions required to support implementation;
- Coordinate specified project inputs identified in the applicable assignment, monitor relevant dependencies and resource constraints, and notify the COAR Focal Point of material issues that may affect delivery. The Consultant may review the status of identified technical, research, and other workstreams and provide recommendations concerning their alignment with agreed project requirements, timelines, and available resources. Responsibility for allocating and managing COAR personnel remains with COAR;
- Coordinate agreed operational and logistical requirements of project implementation, including arrangements for project activities, travel, events, workshops, and other operational needs, and provide recommendations to the relevant COAR focal point where COAR action or approval is required. Any expenditure or commitment on COAR's behalf shall require prior written authorisation;
- Identify and assess implementation challenges, risks, and resource constraints, recommend potential mitigation measures, and refer matters requiring COAR decisions or action to the COAR Focal Point or other designated project contact;
- Coordinate the deliverable review process and submit materials to the persons designated by COAR for any required technical, contractual or organisational approval; and
- Support effective project handover and close-out and coordinate the maintenance of key project decisions, documentation, and records in accordance with the agreed assignment and applicable COAR requirements.
- The Consultant will determine the professional approach, sequencing, and methods used to perform the Services, subject to the agreed scope, deliverables, deadlines, contractual requirements, and reasonable coordination with COAR and relevant project stakeholders.

#### **Financial, Administrative, and Compliance Management**

- Support the development and monitoring of project operating budgets, including expenditure, resource utilisation, forecasts, and project-level financial information, and provide recommendations to the relevant COAR focal point;
- Identify the skills, specialist inputs and external resources reasonably required for delivery and provide recommendations to COAR Focal Point. Decisions concerning the engagement, allocation or management of COAR personnel shall remain exclusively with COAR.;
- Identify financial risks or significant variances and make recommendations to the relevant COAR leadership or Finance personnel regarding appropriate mitigation measures;
- Collaborate with Finance to support timely and accurate invoicing, financial reporting, and other project financial requirements limited to the project information, documentation, and coordination outputs specified in the assignment;
- Support compliance of project implementation with applicable contractual requirements and those COAR policies and procedures reasonably applicable to external consultants and necessary for the proper performance of the Services, including requirements relating to safeguarding, confidentiality, data protection, information security, security, and other applicable legal or contractual requirements; and
- Coordinate the preparation and maintenance of required financial, contractual, administrative, and compliance documentation and engage relevant COAR focal points where specialist guidance or approval is required.

#### **Client and Partner Management**

- Where expressly authorised in the applicable assignment, act as an external project coordination contact for the client, without authority to amend the contract, agree additional services, vary fees or deadlines, or otherwise bind COAR;
- Provide agreed project updates to clients regarding project progress, upcoming activities, risks, challenges, and proposed changes affecting delivery, subject to COAR's contractual and client-management requirements;
- Coordinate the documentation of key client feedback, decisions, approvals, and agreed changes relevant to the assigned Services and communicate such information to the relevant COAR personnel.
- Collaborate with technical and research personnel, where relevant to an agreed assignment, to assess client needs and provide recommendations regarding proposed responses, while ensuring that any commitments communicated by the Consultant remain within the agreed project scope and the Consultant's authority.;
- Coordinate project-level interactions with delivery partners and subcontractors, where applicable and where included in the agreed assignment, while responsibility for contractual engagement, appointment, supervision, and management of such parties remains with COAR or the relevant contracting party; and
- Identify opportunities to strengthen client and partner relationships and support potential future collaboration where relevant to the assigned Services.

#### **Organizational and Business Development**

- Where specifically agreed as part of an assignment, provide professional support to proposal development and other business-development activities relating to the Consultant's areas of expertise, including proposal processes, workplanning, resource planning, budgeting, coordination of inputs, and drafting of relevant proposal sections.
- Support effective handover from proposal development to project implementation when opportunities are awarded where such support forms part of an agreed consultancy assignment;
- Provide information concerning potential follow-on work or collaboration opportunities identified in the course of an accepted assignment, where relevant;
- Communicate with relevant stakeholders where reasonably necessary to complete the agreed deliverables and within the scope of the accepted assignment; and
- Attend such project-specific meetings as the Consultant reasonably considers necessary for the delivery of an accepted assignment or as are expressly identified in the relevant work order.

#### **Contextual and Technical Understanding**

- Apply relevant research and analytical knowledge and methodologies as reasonably necessary to perform the agreed project-management Services;
- Review and consider relevant political, economic, social, humanitarian, and other contextual information necessary to perform the specific assignment; and
- Consider relevant client requirements, donor priorities, response architecture, and institutional or organisational activities to the extent necessary to deliver the agreed outputs.

### Deliverables

For each agreed assignment, and subject to the applicable scope, deliverables, estimated level of effort and timeframe, the Consultant will provide Services intended to support the following project outcomes::

- Project coordination outputs are prepared and provided in accordance with the agreed scope, deadlines, and applicable contractual requirements;
- Project workplans, operating budgets, resource plans, and required project management documentation are prepared, coordinated, or maintained as applicable to the agreed assignment;
- Contractual deliverables are coordinated through the relevant review and approval processes and, where the Consultant is responsible for submission under the agreed assignment, submitted within the applicable deadlines and appropriately documented or archived;
- Required project-level financial, administrative, compliance, client-coordination, and organisational processes are appropriately coordinated or supported within the scope of the agreed assignment; and
- Projects are appropriately supported through handover and/or close-out, with required records and documentation coordinated in accordance with the agreed assignment and applicable COAR requirements.

Specific outputs, deadlines, and estimated consultancy days may be further defined according to individual project assignments. Project assignments may be documented through written assignment instructions, work orders, or other mutually agreed written arrangements specifying the relevant scope of Services, deliverables, deadlines, estimated consultancy days, applicable day rate, and any project-specific travel or expense arrangements.

### Required professional experience and expertise

The Consultant should demonstrate the following professional qualifications and experience relevant to the Services:

- A BA degree in business management, political science, international affairs, public administration, public policy, international development, or a related field;
- A minimum of two years' professional experience managing and implementing client-funded projects;
- Demonstrated experience managing project budgets, workplans, resources, deliverables, and client relationships;
- Experience managing research, analysis, monitoring, assessment, or other evidence-generation projects is highly desirable;
- Experience working with an implementing organization, research organization, UN agency, local or international NGO, consultancy, or similar organization;
- Familiarity with donor/client requirements and donor-funded humanitarian, development, stabilization, peacebuilding, early recovery, and/or related programming environments;
- Demonstrated knowledge of Myanmar;
- Fluency in English;
- Demonstrated professional capability in project planning, coordination, communication, and problem-solving relevant to the agreed Services;
- Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgement, manage competing priorities, and collaborate effectively across multidisciplinary teams; and
- High level of professionalism, discretion, and commitment to confidentiality and where applicable, the Consultant shall comply with the safeguarding, confidentiality, data-protection, information-security, health-and-safety and client-mandated requirements which COAR identifies in writing as applicable to external service providers. For the avoidance of doubt, COAR’s general employee handbook, working-hours, attendance, leave, appraisal, disciplinary and grievance procedures shall not apply

Want to make a positive difference to the future of people and our one shared home, the Earth? Working at WWF could be your opportunity of a lifetime.

All around the world, people are waking up to the deepening crisis of nature loss. A growing realization that nature is our life-support system. And that nobody will be spared from the impacts of its loss. Here at WWF, we are helping to tackle this enormous global challenge.

Our people come from hugely diverse backgrounds and with a variety of expertise, ranging from HR and finance to advocacy and conservation science. We welcome applications from anyone who believes they can help us create a better future for people and wildlife.

**What we do**

We are an independent conservation organization, striving to sustain the natural world for the benefit of people and wildlife. From individuals and communities to business and government, we are part of a growing coalition calling on world leaders to set nature on the path to recovery by 2030. Together, we seek to protect and restore natural habitats, stop the mass extinction of wildlife, and make the way we produce and consume sustainable.

For the needs of its operations, WWF CAR is looking for a Head of Monitoring, Research, Primate Habituation, One Health and Forest Department.

Location: Bayanga, Dzanga Sangha Protected Area, CAR

Contract type: fixed term (2 years renewable)

**Mission:**

The role of this position are to provide technical oversight and leadership to ensure the effective management of the Primate Habituation Programme (PHP), Monitoring, research, animal health/’One Health’ and forest management activities in the Dzanga-Sangha Protected Areas (DSPA), and transfer technical and management knowledge and experience to the DSPA staff.

**Main function and responsibilities:**

Head of Monitoring, Research, Primate Habituation, One Health and Forest Department will:

**Ensures that primate habituation programme (PHP) and related research activities are managed to the highest international standards (approx. 20%):**

- Supervise all aspects of the PHP focussing essentially on Lowland Gorilla and Agile Mangabey;
- Support the PHP Technical Assistant in ensuring the day-to-day operations and management of the PHP, including spending time at field sites in the forest (Bai Hokou and Mongambe);
- Ensure that the habituation process is conducted using a non-invasive methodology that minimises risk (stress, disease, injury, behaviour change) to the primates. Similarly, ensure the risks of injuries and of transmission of disease to visitors, staff and volunteers are minimised;
- Ensure the PHP adheres to IUCN best practise guidelines;
- Maintain and improve digital PHP data collection (Earthranger) and ensure that the various data are properly organised, stored, backed-up, archived and disseminated as needed;
- Support the maintenance of PHP camps (Bai Hokou and Mogambe)

**Promotes and coordinates research and monitoring activities at DSPA (20%):**

- Coordinate all the research programs in DSPA
- Ensure appropriate research procedures are in place (including proposal assessment, permits, methodology, report submission and appropriate acknowledgement etc.);
- Maintain an up-to-date record of all publications and reports emanating from research work carried out at DSPA;
- Maintain the current biomonitoring program that include Bai monitoring, insect monitoring, meteo station, Elephant DNA SCR, water EDNA monitoring and the deployment of a water quality station;
- Coordinate relevant biological data collection by DSPA staff and support the procedure from conception to evaluation;
- In close collaboration with the Elephant listening project maintain monitoring of Dzanga Bai, bioacoustics grid and the development of elephant individual identification tools.
- Conduct and standardize additional impact-monitoring studies related to forest cover change and human wellbeing.
- Contribute to the development and implementation of joint research and monitoring procedures with partners in the Sangha Tri-national Landscape and WWF Regional Bimonitoring Team ;
- Collaborate closely with local partner in the long-term management of the community hunting zone and market study activities.
- Solicit conservation-focused research with external partners (academic, conservation, etc.);

**Oversees the implementation and development of sustainable forest exploitation and restoration approaches (20%)**

- Supervise the forestry work on legal and certified logging and land use plan ;
- Support the forestry responsable in ensuring day to day operations ;
- Maintain and develop the implementation of a forest concession monitoring procedure;
- Support the agroforestry project responsible in ensuring day-to-day operations.
- Support Human Wildife Conflicts mitigation strategy in collaboration with the Local committee of land use management.
- Support the deployment of sustainable cacao and coffee production around DSPA.

**Oversees the implementation and development of One Health monitoring activities (20%)**

- Supervise the One Health work focusing essentially on surveillance of great ape, wildlife and DSPA staff health to reduce risk of zoonotic infectious disease emergence.
- Support the Wildlife Veterinary Officer in ensuring day-to-day operations and management of the One Health work;
- Support the functioning and expansion of the veterinary lab in Bayanga;
- Support the animal sampling protocols (carcasses, great apes, domestic animals, ...)
- Support the deployment of community-based solution in the mitigation of zoonotic risk transmission.

**Transversal tasks (20%):**

- Submit to the Director a monthly and quarterly report outlining programme activities;
- Supervise, train and conduct continuous and annual evaluations of staff under supervision (approximately 80 people);
- Maintain meaningful data collection and visualization tools (dashboards) to help monitor and improve DSPA conservation impact.
- Participate in the elaboration of sustainable development projects including black soldier flies, biogas and sustainable agricultural practices.
- Support others DSPA departments in their data collection tools and procedures to improve activities impacts and strategic planning;
- Contribute to the formulation of DSPA policies;
- Assist the Director in communications, permits and logistics associated with external researchers, volunteers and students.
- Assists the Director to ensure accountability of WWF project funds according to project planning and contractual obligations in collaboration with the F&A Manager;
- Contributes to fund-raising, grant writing and reporting to donors as requested by the Director.

## Others

- Attend international/ regional/ national relevant tourism forums to promote DSPA;
- Work in collaboration with the Communication Department to feed the website with stories around the available tourism opportunities in DSPA;
- Carry out any other duties assigned by the line manager.

### What you need:

**Required Qualifications:**

- A minimum of an MSc in biology, ecology or a related field.
- A minimum of 7 years of experience in working in the field of applied ecological research, including on Primate Habituation and bio-monitoring within a tropical forest environment;
- Professional experience with and/or exposure to forestry, agroforestry and ‘One Health’ projects.
- Extensive knowledge of data collection with Earthrangers (e.g. SMART, Kobocollect) and processing (e.g. MS Office, R-studio, GIS, ArcGIS, …) tools;
- Fluency in both French and English;
- Knowledge of Sango is a plus;
- Coding language is a plus ;
- Depth and breadth knowledge of conservation and development issues;
- Ability to live and work in a remote place.

**Required skills and competences:**

- Good leadership and team work abilities;
- Ability to work under pressure;
- Excellent inter-personal skills, including the ability to develop and maintain strong relationships at all levels, within WWF CAR and, as required, with external stakeholders;
- Excellent oral and written communications skills in English and French;
- High ethics and a personal commitment to transparency and accountability;
- Sensibility on safeguarding standards and social policies (gender, human rights etc.) are expected;
- Ability to work in a remote environment with regular missions offering logistical challenge;
- Adhere to WWF’s values: Courage, Respect, Integrity and Collaboration;
- Demonstrates WWF behaviours in ways of working: Strive for impact, Listen Deeply, Collaborate Openly, Innovate Fearlessly.

### How to apply?

Interested candidates should prepare and submit: a cover letter and a curriculum vitae, all together not exceeding 5 pages to the following e-mail address: recruitment@wwfcar.org

The subject should read “Head of Monitoring, Research, Primate Habituation, One Health and Forest Department ”

Deadline for applications: 15th november 2026

Please note that only candidates under serious consideration will be contacted for follow up. If you have not been contacted six weeks after closing, consider your application unsuccessful.

*WWF is an equal opportunity employer and committed to having a diverse workforce*

**Objetivo del trabajo**

El Oficial de Logístico está a cargo de la gestión logística de ACTED a nivel nacional, asume los roles y funciones actuando dentro de los límites de la autoridad delegada y de conformidad con los procedimientos y directrices del departamento de logística, conforme a las políticas y procedimientos logísticos de ACTED.

## Cadena de mando

Bajo la autoridad de:

